ACL-DP Operational Codebook
=============================

Final scoring definition aligned with the revised manuscript and executable analysis code.

IMPORTANT SCORING NOTE
----------------------
The final ACL-DP composite score contains three scored mechanism families only:
1. Effort Engineering (EE)
2. Attention Engineering (AE)
3. Cognitive Load (CL) Amplification

Adaptive Architecture/Adaptive Behavior (AA), when available in the dataset, is retained as a supplementary descriptive variable and is NOT included in the final ACL-DP composite score.

Accordingly:

ACLDP_TOTAL_SCORE = EFFORT_SCORE + ATTENTION_SCORE + COGNITIVE_LOAD_SCORE

The theoretical range of ACLDP_TOTAL_SCORE is 0-7.

Variable	Definition	Type / Range	Operational rule / scope
Sector_Group	Heuristic domain-based sector classification	categorical	Descriptive grouping variable; not part of ACL-DP scoring.
EFFORT_VALID	Interface has observable accept and reject click counts	binary	1 when both Accept_Click_Count and Reject_Click_Count are observable; EE analyses requiring a rejection pathway are restricted to EFFORT_VALID = 1.
MECH_EE_ClickAsymmetry	Reject path requires more clicks than accept path	binary	1 if EFFORT_VALID = 1 and Reject_Click_Count > Accept_Click_Count; otherwise 0.
MECH_EE_HiddenReject	Reject option is located behind a deeper interaction pathway	binary	1 when the operational audit variable indicates a hidden/deeper reject pathway; otherwise 0.
MECH_AE_PrimaryAccept	Primary action is acceptance	binary	1 when the primary consent action is coded as accept; otherwise 0.
MECH_AE_ProminenceAsymmetry	Accept control is more visually prominent than reject control	binary	1 when Accept_Button_Prominence > Reject_Button_Prominence and both values are observable; otherwise 0.
MECH_CL_HighComplexity	High Layer-2 configuration complexity	binary	Evaluated only for interfaces with an accessible Layer-2 panel; 1 when CL_Toggle_Vendor_Complexity_Index >= 20; otherwise 0.
MECH_CL_HighInfoDensity	High Layer-2 information density	binary	Evaluated only for interfaces with an accessible Layer-2 panel; 1 when L2_Information_Density_Score >= 4; otherwise 0.
MECH_CL_HighToggleVolume	High Layer-2 toggle volume	supplementary binary	Evaluated only for interfaces with an accessible Layer-2 panel; 1 when L2_Toggle_Count >= 10; otherwise 0. This indicator is retained for descriptive/sensitivity purposes and is NOT included in the final COGNITIVE_LOAD_SCORE.
MECH_CL_GermaneSuppression	Suppressed explanatory support within Layer-2 configuration	binary	Evaluated only for interfaces with an accessible Layer-2 panel; 1 when germane-support suppression is coded as present; otherwise 0.
MECH_AA_RePrompting	Re-prompting after rejection is observed	supplementary binary	Retained as a descriptive adaptive-behavior variable when available. It is NOT included in the final ACL-DP mechanism scores or ACLDP_TOTAL_SCORE.

FINAL MECHANISM SCORES
----------------------
EFFORT_SCORE
Definition:
    MECH_EE_ClickAsymmetry + MECH_EE_HiddenReject
Range:
    0-2
Interpretation:
    Higher values indicate a greater number of observable effort-asymmetry indicators.
Analytical scope:
    EE prevalence and mechanism-specific analyses requiring an observable rejection pathway should use the EFFORT_VALID subset.

ATTENTION_SCORE
Definition:
    MECH_AE_PrimaryAccept + MECH_AE_ProminenceAsymmetry
Range:
    0-2
Interpretation:
    Higher values indicate a greater number of observable attention-engineering indicators.

COGNITIVE_LOAD_SCORE
Definition:
    MECH_CL_HighComplexity
    + MECH_CL_HighInfoDensity
    + MECH_CL_GermaneSuppression
Range:
    0-3
Interpretation:
    Higher values indicate a greater number of observable Layer-2 interface conditions used as proxies for cognitive-load amplification.
Analytical scope:
    CL indicators are evaluated only within interfaces with an accessible Layer-2 panel.
Construct-validity note:
    These indicators are interface-level proxies. They characterize observable complexity, information density, and explanatory-support conditions; they do not directly measure users' experienced cognitive workload.

ACLDP_TOTAL_SCORE
Definition:
    EFFORT_SCORE + ATTENTION_SCORE + COGNITIVE_LOAD_SCORE
Range:
    0-7
Interpretation:
    Additive composite summarizing the scored EE, AE, and CL interface-level indicators.
Important:
    The total score is mathematically constructed from its component mechanism scores. Correlations between component scores and ACLDP_TOTAL_SCORE are therefore part-whole associations and should not be interpreted as independent construct-validation evidence.

FINAL EXCLUSIONS FROM THE COMPOSITE SCORE
-----------------------------------------
- MECH_CL_HighToggleVolume is not included in COGNITIVE_LOAD_SCORE.
- MECH_AA_RePrompting / Adaptive Architecture is not included in ACLDP_TOTAL_SCORE.
- No ADAPTIVITY_SCORE is included in the final composite scoring definition.

MECHANISM-SPECIFIC DENOMINATORS
-------------------------------
- Interface-level and AE analyses: observable consent-interface sample.
- EE analyses requiring an observable rejection pathway: EFFORT_VALID subset.
- CL analyses: accessible Layer-2 subset.

These scope restrictions should be preserved when reporting sample-specific percentages and should not be interpreted as population-level prevalence estimates.
